1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,572
Coach: The task can change while the need for an accurate shared account remains.

2
00:00:05,572 --> 00:00:07,714
Coach: Here is a fresh example:

3
00:00:07,714 --> 00:00:13,715
Coach: a walking group needs one printed notice with meeting details and a bring-list.

4
00:00:13,715 --> 00:00:17,143
Coach: We are no longer arranging a taster session,

5
00:00:17,143 --> 00:00:21,429
Coach: and no earlier proposal or agreement carries into this case.

6
00:00:21,779 --> 00:00:25,208
Coach: Maya wants the meeting details at the top.

7
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:29,493
Coach: Noah proposes a short checklist using the existing bring-list.

8
00:00:29,493 --> 00:00:33,351
Coach: The details themselves are supplied to that fictional group,

9
00:00:33,351 --> 00:00:36,351
Coach: but their length is not given here.

10
00:00:36,351 --> 00:00:41,494
Coach: Keep them as labelled content blocks instead of inventing a meeting time,

11
00:00:41,494 --> 00:00:43,208
Coach: place or required item.

12
00:00:43,558 --> 00:00:45,701
Maya: I support keeping the checklist.

13
00:00:45,701 --> 00:00:49,987
Maya: I would still put the meeting details at the top.

14
00:00:50,337 --> 00:00:53,337
Noah: I support making the meeting details prominent.

15
00:00:53,337 --> 00:00:58,051
Noah: Can we check that both parts stay readable on one page?

16
00:01:06,401 --> 00:01:08,544
Coach: The contributions can be connected

17
00:01:08,544 --> 00:01:11,972
Coach: because the page needs both kinds of information.

18
00:01:11,972 --> 00:01:15,401
Coach: That does not mean every possible layout fits.

19
00:01:15,401 --> 00:01:19,258
Coach: The exact content length and readability still need checking.

20
00:01:19,258 --> 00:01:22,687
Coach: A compact summary can preserve the shared direction

21
00:01:22,687 --> 00:01:25,258
Coach: while leaving that practical question open.

22
00:01:25,608 --> 00:01:29,894
You: There is support for prominent meeting details and a checklist.

23
00:01:29,894 --> 00:01:32,894
You: We could try them on one page,

24
00:01:32,894 --> 00:01:35,894
You: then check readability before choosing the layout.

25
00:01:36,244 --> 00:01:40,530
Coach: This model reports the supported direction and proposes a test.

26
00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:46,530
Coach: It does not say that the page has been laid out, checked or approved.

27
00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:54,244
Coach: If the content does not fit, the group would need a revision that preserves the essential printed information,

28
00:01:54,244 --> 00:01:58,530
Coach: not an unsupported claim that a link solves the problem.

29
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,166
Coach: Notice what transferred:

30
00:02:12,166 --> 00:02:15,594
Coach: keep ownership clear, retain the scope of support,

31
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:19,451
Coach: connect compatible purposes and name what still needs checking.

32
00:02:19,451 --> 00:02:22,451
Coach: The content and the relevant constraint changed.

33
00:02:22,451 --> 00:02:26,737
Coach: You did not need to copy the book-club sequence

34
00:02:26,737 --> 00:02:30,594
Coach: or force time calculations onto a page-layout task.

35
00:02:30,944 --> 00:02:35,658
Coach: Before your next group summary, choose one question to ask yourself.

36
00:02:35,658 --> 00:02:38,230
Coach: Am I reporting what was said?

37
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:41,230
Coach: Have I turned a condition into agreement?

38
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:44,658
Coach: Is my next step proposed or already decided?

39
00:02:44,658 --> 00:02:47,658
Coach: Use the question that fits the moment,

40
00:02:47,658 --> 00:02:51,515
Coach: then let the group's actual reply determine what changes.
